// # WASM-WAVE — Classify the 19 wasm_*.oot files into four waves
//
// Logline: 19 audit files split into Wave A master phalanx (1), Wave B COORD if-fold review (7), Wave C Loop-12 five-folds (5), and Wave D shared/runtime (6), with file:line evidence and a no-merge verdict.
//
// Setup: Static read of every wasm_*.oot under openOODA/audit/ and the entry wasm_emit*.oo under ooda/oodac/. Pin: v0.205.0-beta. C emit + gcc everyday. Browser WASM host residual. Time anchors come from the audit files themselves; no dates invented.
//
// Beats:
//   1. List the 19 files and assign each to exactly one wave.
//   2. Quote each wave's master plan, expected deliverable, and on-disk status.
//   3. Name the cross-wave drifts and the on-disk evidence.
//   4. Recommend keep-separate; explain why merge would break isolation.

## 0. Verdict

  KEEP SEPARATE. Four waves, four scopes, disjoint write
  sets. Wave A is the master plan. Wave B is a coordinated
  if-fold review with a parent-rebuild gate. Wave C is a
  5-fold Loop-12 cycle. Wave D is the runtime / shared lane.
  Merging B and D drops the no-two-roles-share-a-write rule
  (wasm_coord.oot:62). Merging C into B mixes the 5-fold
  cycle into the 1-fold review.
