## 2. Wave A — 12-role master phalanx (1 file)

  Scope: name every owner and the disjoint file set so
  emit-wasm can write one real print body for `main`.
  Ship bar is `Hello, openOODA!` literal plus WASI
  `fd_write`.

  Master plan: openOODA/audit/wasm_phalanx.oot lines 1-88.
  Ship bar lines 9-14. Frozen API lines 17-35. File
  ownership lines 39-71. Forbidden list lines 74-78.

  12 roles and their audit files (per wasm_phalanx.oot:39-71):
    DE1 -> wasm_de1.oot; DE2 -> wasm_de2.oot (line 43)
    RT  -> wasm_rt.oot (line 46); PV1 -> wasm_pv1.oot
    PV2 -> wasm_pv2.oot (line 54); SEC -> wasm_sec.oot
    MEM -> wasm_mem.oot; INT -> wasm_int.oot (line 60)
    HARN-> wasm_harn.oot (line 61); HYG -> wasm_hyg.oot
    DOCS-> wasm_docs.oot; COORD-> wasm_coord.oot (line 71)
  Actual: written. Line 5 names "leftover". Line 78 forbids
  browser host. Re-org is left to COORD.
## 3. Wave B — COORD-wave, if-fold review (7 files)

  Scope: re-org the 12-role phalanx so a single parent
  rebuild precedes a fan-out review of if-fold fixtures,
  existing locks, ovf/buf/dummy/fold/two/int, line counts,
  and boards. If-fold is the new beat; parent rebuild gates.

  Master plan: openOODA/audit/wasm_coord.oot lines 1-225.
  Wave intro lines 18-30. Parent rebuild lines 32-41. Role
  table lines 46-60. If-fixture review lines 67-100. INT
  locks lines 102-128. SEC/MEM/RT lines 130-145. DE1/DE2
  lines 147-156. HYG lines 158-165. DOCS/PV2 lines 167-179.
  Order lines 191-202. Residual lines 204-216.

  7 files and what they did:
    wasm_coord.oot   COORD wave file. Write set is this
                     file only (lines 183-189).
    wasm_de1.oot     DE1 re-read of wasm_emit_fold.oo.
                     Status at line 130. Extra println
                     misses (line 92).
    wasm_de2.oot     DE2 re-read of wasm_emit_two.oo
                     and wasm_emit_int.oo. Status at 181.
    wasm_harn.oot    HARN if-true review. Body lines
                     19-25. Magic lock lines 41-48.
    wasm_harn2.oot   HARN2 if-false review. Body lines
                     19-25. wasmtime required line 43.
    wasm_pv1.oot     PV1 hostile IDENT if. Verdict PASS
                     line 16. Condition proof 53-77.
    wasm_pv2.oot     PV2 board honesty. Verdict lines
                     14-29. Quotes S1/S2/R1/R2 lines
                     33-86.

  Drift inside Wave B: wasm_coord.oot:46-60 names 14 owners
  including Parent, not 13 audit files. HARN2 is a Wave B
  addition; the master phalanx did not name it.

## 4. Wave C — Loop-12, five advanced folds (5 files)

  Scope: extend the if-fold to five more const-print shapes:
  seventeen println, paren-not-eq no-else, neq-or no-else,
  paren-neq-and no-else, lt-and no-else. Each shape has one
  hit detector plus one IDENT hostile.

  Master plan: openOODA/audit/wasm_arch.oot lines 1-15.
  Five folds at lines 6-10. Hostiles at line 12. Adjacent
  pipelines off-limits at line 14.

  5 files and what they did:
    wasm_arch.oot    Arch lead. Status BAR line 16.
    wasm_pipe.oot    Pipeline. Five detector files at
                     lines 5-9. Status at line 14.
    wasm_qa.oot      QA. Five hits lines 12-16. Five
                     hostiles lines 20-24. Drive line 27.
    wasm_sk1.oot     SK1 false-fold hunt. Verdict line
                     11. Five shapes lines 15-33.
    wasm_sk2.oot     SK2 isolation. Verdict line 12.

  On-disk evidence: Loop-12 detectors are imported by
  wasm_emit_pick_if.oo. Lines 32, 45, 63, 64, 65 list:
  wasm_emit_seventeen.oo, wasm_emit_ifpneqne.oo,
  wasm_emit_ifneqorne.oo, wasm_emit_ifpneqandne.oo,
  wasm_emit_ifltandne.oo. wasm_pipe.oot:5-9 names the
  same five files. Match.

